@startuml descriptor-kinds-overview
' Entity view of the charter descriptor kinds and how they relate: the decided design.
' Decided design: ADR-0048 (composition), ADR-0049 (glossary), ADR-0050 (mission types, lifecycles, gates),
' ADR-0051 (event registry), ADR-0052 (anti-patterns). Accepted 2026-11-02; none of it is built yet.
' Sources (core repo spec-kitty, read-only), for the parts that stay as they are:
'   src/charter/offering/artifact_kinds.py         (ArtifactKind)
'   src/charter/offering/drg/models.py             (NodeKind, Relation, DRGNode, DRGEdge)
'   src/charter/offering/packs/pack_descriptor.py  (PackDescriptor, pack.yaml)
'   src/charter/activation/schemas.py              (GovernanceCharterConfig selected_*)
' Built-in edge counts are not drawn: they are today's data, not the design.
' Pending: a yellow <<pending>> entity or a [pending ADR-00xx OQn] suffix marks a part whose open question is not ruled.
!include _style.iuml
title Charter descriptor kinds — decided design (ADR-0048…ADR-0052)

package "Charter Pack (pack.yaml)" as pack {
  entity "PackDescriptor" as PD <<authored>> {
    pack_id
    name
    pack_level : PackTier <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0048 OQ7: required?]</color>
    parent_pack : ref? [lineage only]
    depends_on : {pack_id, range}[] <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0048 OQ4]</color>
    pack_drg : path?
  }
  entity "PackDescriptor\n(the parent pack)" as PDP <<authored>>
  entity "PackManifest" as PM <<generated>>
  entity "DRG fragment\n(*.graph.yaml | drg/fragment.yaml)" as FRAG {
    schema_version = "1.0"
    nodes : DRGNode[]
    edges : DRGEdge[]
  }
  entity "Preset\n(presets/<id>.yaml)" as PS {
    activated_<plural> : {id, must_have?}[]
  }
}

package "Descriptor kinds (one YAML file per artifact)" as kinds {
  entity Directive
  entity Tactic
  entity Paradigm
  entity Styleguide
  entity Toolguide
  entity Procedure
  entity AgentProfile
  entity MissionStepContract
  entity MissionType <<ordinary kind>> {
    steps (transitions, guards, actions)
  }
  entity Lifecycle {
    states, transitions, guards
    <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ4]</color>
  }
  entity "Glossary\n(a context)" as Glossary {
    glossary:<id> <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ3]</color>
  }
  entity AntiPattern <<activatable>>
  entity EventRegistry <<kind>> {
    not activatable <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0051 OQ1]</color>
    not a CRG node <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0051 OQ3]</color>
  }
  entity Gate <<pending>> {
    <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ2]</color>
  }
  entity StepEnhancement <<pending>> {
    <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ7, OQ8]</color>
  }
  entity PackSkill
  entity "Template / Asset" as TA <<not activatable>>
}

entity "term" as Term <<node-only>> {
  term:<context-id>/<term-id>
}

entity "GovernanceCharterConfig\n(project charter)" as GC {
  selected_<plural> : id[]
}

PD "1" *-- "1" PM : sibling
PD "1" *-- "0..1" FRAG : pack_drg
PD "1" *-- "0..*" PS : presets/
PD "1" o-- "*" kinds : ships
PD "*" --> "*" PD : depends_on\n(versioned range)\n<color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0048 OQ4, OQ6]</color>
PD ..> PDP : parent_pack\n(lineage only)
FRAG ..> kinds : DRGNode.urn = kind:id
PS ..> kinds : activates; must_have items\nare the required floor (ADR-0031)
GC ..> kinds : selects (selected_* per activatable kind)

' Containment inside a mission type's bundle, and links between kinds
MissionType "1" o-- "*" MissionStepContract : bundle (step_contracts/)
MissionType ..> Lifecycle : work_package_lifecycle\n(on a step)\n<color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ5]</color>
MissionType ..> Gate : guard {gate, config}
Lifecycle ..> Gate : guard {gate, config}
MissionType ..> EventRegistry : emit resolves against\n(the depends_on closure)
Lifecycle ..> EventRegistry : emit resolves against
StepEnhancement ..> MissionType : target action:<type>/<step>\n(adds guidance, guards, emit)\n<color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ7, OQ8]</color>
MissionType ..> Term : terms (term: URNs)\n<color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ10]</color>
Glossary "1" *-- "1..*" Term : terms inside a context
' Guidance rejects an anti-pattern (Relation.rejects), never suggests
Directive ..> AntiPattern : rejects
Tactic ..> AntiPattern : rejects
Paradigm ..> AntiPattern : rejects
Styleguide ..> AntiPattern : rejects
Procedure ..> AntiPattern : rejects
MissionType ..> AntiPattern : rejects

' DRG edges (DRGEdge.relation): illustrative pairs, not exhaustive, no counts
Tactic --> Tactic : suggests
AgentProfile --> Directive : requires / suggests
AgentProfile --> Tactic : requires
Directive --> Tactic : suggests
Procedure --> Tactic : requires
Paradigm --> Directive : requires
AgentProfile --> AgentProfile : specializes_from
' Model-level links (fields)
MissionStepContract ..> AgentProfile : steps[].delegates_to\n(kind + candidates)
PackSkill ..> PackSkill : enhances / overrides (fields)

note bottom of kinds
  Relation enum (drg/models.py): requires, suggests, applies, scope,
  vocabulary, instantiates, replaces, delegates_to, specializes_from,
  enhances, overrides, refines, in_tension_with, reconciles_tension, rejects.
  vocabulary targets glossary and term (ADR-0049 d4).
  A step enhancement is a file, not the enhances relation (ADR-0050 d22).
end note
legend right
  <<authored>> hand-edited; <<generated>> machine-written.
  Solid diamond = file containment; dashed = id/URN reference.
  Yellow <<pending>> / [pending …]: decided in the cited ADR,
  but the cited open question is not ruled.
endlegend
@enduml
